.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH pgloupe-logs-report 1  "report " 
.SH NAME
pgloupe\-logs\-report \- Report on a time window of a store
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpgloupe logs report\fR [\fB\-\-slowest\fR] [\fB\-\-since\fR] [\fB\-\-until\fR] [\fB\-\-by\fR] [\fB\-\-top\fR] [\fB\-\-bucket\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-store\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Report on a time window of a store
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-store\fR \fI<STORE>\fR
The store file written by `logs ingest`
.TP
\fB\-\-slowest\fR \fI<SLOWEST>\fR
Slowest executions to list, at most what the ingest kept (20 unless it was told more)
.TP
\fB\-\-since\fR \fI<SINCE>\fR
Start of the window (RFC 3339 or `YYYY\-MM\-DD`, UTC); rounded down to the hour
.TP
\fB\-\-until\fR \fI<UNTIL>\fR
End of the window; rounded up to the hour
.TP
\fB\-\-by\fR \fI<BY>\fR [default: total]
Metric that orders the statement table
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
total: Total execution time
.IP \(bu 2
calls: Number of calls
.IP \(bu 2
p95: 95th percentile of the duration
.IP \(bu 2
max: Slowest single call
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-top\fR \fI<TOP>\fR [default: 20]
Statements to list (`all` for every statement)
.TP
\fB\-\-bucket\fR \fI<BUCKET>\fR [default: 1m]
Timeline resolution: a multiple of one minute
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR [default: text]
Report format
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
text
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
